From: RTSP-on-GE contributors
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Admit canonical MJPG through the existing video decoder

The pinned FFmpeg already decodes MJPEG and its RIFF table maps MJPG to
AV_CODEC_ID_MJPEG. Admit canonical MFVideoFormat_MJPG in the existing
WMV-backed video MFT and DMO, as used for Theora, AV1, VP8/9 and HEVC.
Preserve every existing input/output entry and its order.

Do not canonicalize container-specific MJPEG tags. Some carry decoder
semantics (MTSJ changes chroma order; MJPG influences interlace handling).
Ordinary AVI MJPG and the existing tag-absent RIFF fallback already publish
the canonical subtype. Noncanonical jpeg/mjpa/MTSJ variants remain outside
this new public admission instead of losing their original tags.

This is ordinary demux-framed MJPG admission, not Motion JPEG-B, GIF/APNG,
fragment assembly, hardware decoding, a parser, HDR or a new output path.
Existing decode, conversion, timestamps, flush and output validation remain
unchanged. Source tests do not replace candidate public-MF playback tests.

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/video_decoder.c
@@ -2535,6 +2535,7 @@
     &MFVideoFormat_VP90,
     &MFVideoFormat_VP80,
     &MFVideoFormat_HEVC,
+    &MFVideoFormat_MJPG,
 };
 static const GUID *const wmv_decoder_output_types[] =
 {
diff --git a/dlls/wmvdecod/wmvdecod.c b/dlls/wmvdecod/wmvdecod.c
--- a/dlls/wmvdecod/wmvdecod.c
+++ b/dlls/wmvdecod/wmvdecod.c
@@ -71,6 +71,7 @@
         {MFMediaType_Video, MFVideoFormat_VP90},
         {MFMediaType_Video, MFVideoFormat_VP80},
         {MFMediaType_Video, MFVideoFormat_HEVC},
+        {MFMediaType_Video, MFVideoFormat_MJPG},
     };
     MFT_REGISTER_TYPE_INFO wmv_decoder_mft_outputs[] =
     {
@@ -115,6 +116,7 @@
         {.type = MEDIATYPE_Video, .subtype = MFVideoFormat_VP90},
         {.type = MEDIATYPE_Video, .subtype = MFVideoFormat_VP80},
         {.type = MEDIATYPE_Video, .subtype = MFVideoFormat_HEVC},
+        {.type = MEDIATYPE_Video, .subtype = MFVideoFormat_MJPG},
     };
     HRESULT hr;
 
